                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "disused",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "89536197-0306-3d87-a617-a46cb1f413ce",
                                        "entry_id": "490ae4bc-1da5-3191-936b-d38679def613",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "No longer in use."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "not-comparable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d93aa482-9f9a-4634-b19c-ea83302467a5",
                                                "sense_id": "89536197-0306-3d87-a617-a46cb1f413ce",
                                                "text": "But as time & experience do reforme euery thing that is amisse, so this bitter poeme called the old Comedy, being disused and taken away, the new Comedy came in place, more ciuill and pleasant a great deale and not touching any man by name, but in a certain generalitie glancing at euery abuse,"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "edf6faf2-d9ae-42c7-9d39-6c7979a4798e",
                                                "sense_id": "89536197-0306-3d87-a617-a46cb1f413ce",
                                                "text": "In Scotland the custom, now disused in England, of inviting the relations of the deceased to the interment is universally retained."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "69d240bd-b0e3-464d-b858-05bf7548805b",
                                                "sense_id": "89536197-0306-3d87-a617-a46cb1f413ce",
                                                "text": "And now Love sang: but his was such a song,\nSo meshed with half-remembrance hard to free,\nAs souls disused in death’s sterility\nMay sing when the new birthday tarries long."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3fa24773-9a64-4968-b843-712c1aba417e",
                                                "sense_id": "89536197-0306-3d87-a617-a46cb1f413ce",
                                                "text": "The breath that stirred his lips he soon resigned\nTo windy chaos, and we only find\nThe garnered husks of his disusèd words."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d4af7814-bff9-49c4-9c55-4eb9492b080f",
                                                "sense_id": "89536197-0306-3d87-a617-a46cb1f413ce",
                                                "text": "The tables, for instance, were to be covered with baize, but when the patron found that baize was expensive he bought instead disused army blankets, smelling incorrigibly of sweat."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2b08061e-83bb-4266-8ca7-4cb98d756ce3",
                                                "sense_id": "89536197-0306-3d87-a617-a46cb1f413ce",
                                                "text": "It was to assist in the filling-in of the tunnel on the disused Patricroft-Clifton Junction line, which was the scene of a disaster in 1953 when part, below some houses in Swinton, caved in."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d20e5b2d-c447-49f1-8d26-ca7e79512857",
                                                "sense_id": "89536197-0306-3d87-a617-a46cb1f413ce",
                                                "text": "[…] the disused, wrecked Byzantine churches that brooded, forlorn, lovely, ravished and apostate ghosts, about the hills and shores of that lost empire."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8107b4ef-3e4b-4fe4-8db0-3c75d6d65184",
                                                "sense_id": "89536197-0306-3d87-a617-a46cb1f413ce",
                                                "text": "All around in shadow lurked the shapes of trunks, wooden boxes, furniture, disused and broken."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "059388e8-af56-45b5-b28e-79dc56d51b02",
                                                "sense_id": "89536197-0306-3d87-a617-a46cb1f413ce",
                                                "text": "The old station buildings and train shed at Redcar Central were taken out of use around 30 years ago and became a business centre, but are currently disused. Redcar & Cleveland Council has plans to improve the station, including better passenger facilities and retail units."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
